# ⚙️ Prerequisites

Install the following:

* Git
* Node.js
* npm
* Docker
* Jenkins
* AWS EC2 Ubuntu Server

---

# 📥 Clone Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Pathan-Rahaman-Khan/Todo_app_With_Jenkins.git

cd Todo_app_With_Jenkins
```

---

# ▶️ Run Application Locally

## Install Dependencies

```bash
npm install
```

## Start Application

```bash
npm start
```

## Open Browser

```text
http://localhost:3000
```

---

# 🐳 Docker Setup

## Build Docker Image

```bash
docker build -t todo-app .
```

## Verify Image

```bash
docker images
```

## Run Docker Container

```bash
docker run -d \
--name todo-container \
-p 3000:3000 \
todo-app
```

## Verify Running Container

```bash
docker ps
```

## View Logs

```bash
docker logs -f todo-container
```

## Stop Container

```bash
docker stop todo-container
```

## Remove Container

```bash
docker rm todo-container
```

---

# ☁️ AWS EC2 Setup

## Launch EC2 Instance

Recommended:

```text
Ubuntu Server 24.04 LTS
```

## Open Security Group Ports

| Port | Purpose          |
| ---- | ---------------- |
| 22   | SSH              |
| 8080 | Jenkins          |
| 3000 | Todo Application |

---

# ☕ Install Java

```bash
sudo apt update

sudo apt install -y fontconfig openjdk-21-jre

java --version
```

---

# 🔧 Install Jenkins

## Add Jenkins Repository Key

```bash
sudo wget -O /etc/apt/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc \
https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable/jenkins.io-2026.key
```

## Add Repository

```bash
echo "deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc] https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable binary/" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/jenkins.list > /dev/null
```

## Install Jenkins

```bash
sudo apt update

sudo apt install -y jenkins
```

## Start Jenkins

```bash
sudo systemctl enable jenkins

sudo systemctl start jenkins
```

## Verify Status

```bash
sudo systemctl status jenkins
```

## Get Initial Password

```bash
sudo cat /var/lib/jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword
```

---

# 🔑 GitHub SSH Configuration

## Generate SSH Key

```bash
ssh-keygen
```

## View Public Key

```bash
cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
```

Add this key in:

```text
GitHub
→ Settings
→ SSH and GPG Keys
→ New SSH Key
```

---

# 🐳 Install Docker

```bash
sudo apt update

sudo apt install -y docker.io
```

## Start Docker

```bash
sudo systemctl start docker

sudo systemctl enable docker
```

## Add Jenkins User to Docker Group

```bash
sudo usermod -aG docker jenkins

sudo systemctl restart jenkins
```

## Verify Docker

```bash
docker --version

docker ps
```

---

# ⚙️ Jenkins Configuration

## Source Code Management

Select:

```text
Git
```

Repository URL:

```text
git@github.com:Pathan-Rahaman-Khan/Todo_app_With_Jenkins.git
```

Branch:

```text
*/main
```

---

# 🔔 Build Triggers

Enable:

```text
GitHub hook trigger for GITScm polling
```

---

# 🚀 Execute Shell

Paste below in Jenkins Build Step:

```bash
#!/bin/bash

echo "Building Docker Image..."

docker build -t todo-app .

echo "Stopping Existing Container..."

docker stop todo-container || true

docker rm todo-container || true

echo "Starting New Container..."

docker run -d \
--name todo-container \
-p 3000:3000 \
todo-app

docker ps

echo "Deployment Successful"
```

---

# 🔗 GitHub Webhook Configuration

Open:

```text
GitHub Repository
→ Settings
→ Webhooks
→ Add Webhook
```

Configuration:

```text
Payload URL:
http://<EC2-PUBLIC-IP>:8080/github-webhook/

Content Type:
application/json

Events:
Just the push event

Active:
✓ Checked
```

Example:

```text
http://3.109.154.36:8080/github-webhook/
```

